Bill Bejeck resolved KAFKA-20753.
---------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

> Transactional RocksDB store fails to reopen with transactional status mar=
ker in EOS
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------=
----------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-20753
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20753
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Bug
>          Components: streams
>    Affects Versions: 4.4.0
>            Reporter: Bill Bejeck
>            Assignee: Nicholas Telford
>            Priority: Blocker
>             Fix For: 4.4.0
>
>
> -With {{processing.guarantee=3Dexactly_once_v2}} and {{enable.transaction=
al.statestores=3Dtrue,}} a rebalance that adds a StreamThread can transient=
ly co-locate the same task's active and standby on one- =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=
=A0 =C2=A0
> =C2=A0 -instance (different threads). The freshly-assigned active opens t=
he persistent RocksDB store while the live sibling standby still holds it o=
pen, so the store-open status check rejects it and the task enters a {{Task=
Corrupted =E2=86=92 re-init =E2=86=92 corrupt}} loop.-
> When=C2=A0{{{}enable.transactional.statestores=3Dtrue{}}}, the KIP-1035 o=
pen/closed
> status marker written to the RocksDB offsets column family on=C2=A0{{open=
()}}
> and=C2=A0{{close()}}=C2=A0was being routed through=C2=A0{{{}Transactional=
DBAccessor.put(){}}},
> which stages writes in the in-memory=C2=A0{{{}RocksDBTransactionBuffer{}}=
}. The
> buffer is discarded without committing on store close, so the CLOSED
> marker was silently lost. The on-disk status remained permanently at
> OPEN, causing every subsequent=C2=A0{{open()}}=C2=A0under EOS
> ({{{}ignoreInvalidState=3Dfalse{}}}) to throw=C2=A0{{{}ProcessorStateExce=
ption("Invalid state during store open..."){}}}, which escalated to
> {{{}TaskCorruptedException{}}}. Because the wipe-and-restore cycle would
> reproduce the same condition, this created an unrecoverable loop



