Hi all,

Just to let you know, we made a small change in the PR compared to what was
written in the KIP.

Instead of setting the output partition to 0 in single-partition mode, we
keep -1.
The reason is that setting it to 0 would break existing user tests that
compare output records using equals(), because the expected record built
from a partition-less constructor defaults to -1.

The KIP has been updated to reflect this.

No re-vote needed of course, just flagging it for transparency.

Thanks

