Ashwin Pankaj resolved KAFKA-20032.
-----------------------------------
      Reviewer: Manikumar
    Resolution: Fixed

> KIP-1265 : Mechanism for automatic detection of internal API usage
> ------------------------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-20032
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20032
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Improvement
>          Components: documentation
>            Reporter: Ashwin Pankaj
>            Assignee: Ashwin Pankaj
>            Priority: Major
>             Fix For: 4.4.0
>
>
> Apache Kafka lacks a concrete, centralized definition of what constitutes a public API. The most relevant information currently available is found [here|https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=50859233#KafkaImprovementProposals-Whatisconsidereda%22majorchange%22thatneedsaKIP].
> Without formal definition or guardrails, there is a risk that builders may inadvertently import internal classes leading to possible build breakages when they compile against a newer Kafka version



