Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20774) ScramDelta.apply() drops SCRAM users
 when processing REMOVE records for absent users or multiple removals in one
 batch
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Mikhail Fomichev (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Mikhail Fomichev created KAFKA-20774:
----------------------------------------

             Summary: ScramDelta.apply() drops SCRAM users when processing =
REMOVE records for absent users or multiple removals in one batch
                 Key: KAFKA-20774
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20774
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: kraft
            Reporter: Mikhail Fomichev


h3. Problem

In KRaft mode,=C2=A0{{ScramDelta.apply()}}=C2=A0can incorrectly remove SCRA=
M credentials from the metadata image when applying a metadata batch.

A typical failing batch for the same=C2=A0{{ScramMechanism}}=C2=A0contains:
 # several=C2=A0{{RemoveUserScramCredentialRecord}}=C2=A0entries for users=
=C2=A0not present=C2=A0in the current=C2=A0{{{}ScramImage{}}};
 # followed by a=C2=A0{{UserScramCredentialRecord}}=C2=A0UPSERT for a user =
that=C2=A0should remain=C2=A0(e.g.=C2=A0{{user-admin}}=C2=A0used for inter-=
broker authentication).

In production, entire SCRAM user sets were lost from broker metadata.
h3. Steps to reproduce

Minimal unit-test reproduction:
{code:java}
ScramDelta delta =3D new ScramDelta(ScramImage.EMPTY);
delta.replay(remove("producer-kcwc", SCRAM_SHA_256));
delta.replay(remove("consumer-xyff", SCRAM_SHA_256));
delta.replay(upsert("user-admin", SCRAM_SHA_256));
delta.replay(remove("update_user_standalone_eryz", SCRAM_SHA_256));
delta.replay(remove("ext-user-dfrx", SCRAM_SHA_256));
delta.replay(upsert("cluster-admin", SCRAM_SHA_512));
ScramImage result =3D delta.apply();
// only user-admin is missing with the broken apply() logic {code}
=C2=A0
h3. Expected behavior

No silent loss of users:=C2=A0after=C2=A0{{{}ScramDelta.apply(){}}}, every =
user that should still exist in metadata=C2=A0must remain=C2=A0in the resul=
ting=C2=A0{{{}ScramImage{}}}. Users must not disappear as a side effect of =
batch ordering, absent REMOVE records, or mechanism cleanup.
h3. Actual behavior

{{user-admin}}=C2=A0disappears from metadata (depends on the order in which=
 changes are processed).
h3. Root cause

In=C2=A0[{{metadata/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/image/ScramDelta.java}}|=
https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/trunk/metadata/src/main/java/org/apach=
e/kafka/image/ScramDelta.java#L82], method=C2=A0{{{}apply(){}}}:
 # REMOVE is applied even when the user is not in=C2=A0{{{}userMap{}}}:

{code:java}
userMap.remove(userName);
if (userMap.isEmpty()) {
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 newMechanisms.remove(mechanism); =C2=A0// fires on an empty m=
ap
}{code}
On an empty base image, each absent REMOVE removes the mechanism from=C2=A0=
{{{}newMechanisms{}}}; a subsequent UPSERT may write into a=C2=A0detached=
=C2=A0{{userMap}}=C2=A0no longer referenced by=C2=A0{{{}newMechanisms{}}}.
=C2=A0

 # {{userMap.isEmpty()}}=C2=A0is checked inside the per-user loop =E2=80=94=
 when multiple REMOVEs are processed in one batch, the mechanism can be dro=
pped early and users that should survive are lost.

h3. Proposed fix

Move after=C2=A0the loop over all user changes.
{code:java}
if (userMap.isEmpty()) newMechanisms.remove(mechanism) {code}
=C2=A0
h3. Kafka version

4.x.x

