Hi Kamal,

CCing you here since I noticed that you were a key reviewer of
KIP-1023 design and implementation. Since this KIP directly addresses
the leader election risk that KIP-1023 identified when the follower
bootstraps from the last tiered offset, I wanted to ask for your
review here.

This KIP uses two configs (leader.election.eligible.local.log.ms and
leader.election.eligible.local.log.bytes) to let the controller
deprioritize replicas with insufficient local data during leader
election.

Do you have any feedback for the proposal? Appreciate your guidance.

Thanks,
Tom

