Chia-Ping Tsai resolved KAFKA-20746.
------------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

> NPE in MetadataCache#toCluster
> ------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-20746
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20746
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Bug
>    Affects Versions: 4.2.0, 4.3.1
>            Reporter: Luke Chen
>            Assignee: Kuan Po Tseng
>            Priority: Blocker
>             Fix For: 4.4.0, 4.2.2, 4.3.2
>
>
> In KAFKA-18225, we fix a bug to allow `ClientQuotaCallback#updateClusterM=
etadata` to be supported in KRaft mode. But the cluster object generated in=
 MetadataCache could cause NPE. See [https://github.com/strimzi/kafka-quota=
s-plugin/issues/71] for more info.
> =C2=A0
> I think the root cause is that in toCluster method, we filter out the fen=
ced brokers to build brokerToNodes map [here|https://github.com/apache/kafk=
a/blob/4.3.1/metadata/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/metadata/MetadataCache=
.java#L151-L154]. But later, we want to get all the replicas info, which in=
clude the fenced replicas, via the filtered brokerToNodes map. So it causes=
 the NPE. That's my assumption because from the original reported bug, we d=
on't have other info. But it's a possible way to cause NPE. We should also =
think if there is other possibility to cause NPE here.=C2=A0



--
