  Hi Federico and all,

 I have just posted a detailed update to the discussion thread regarding
VK12 (offset-sync data loss) and VK10 (namespace collisions).

 Because both of these items are directly tied to critical data safety and
operational stability during failover, I do not believe the KIP is ready
for a vote in its current state. Let's finish addressing these remaining
design gaps in the discussion thread first.

Regards,
Vaquar Khan
https://www.linkedin.com/in/vaquar-khan-b695577/

On Wed, 8 Jul 2026 at 07:16, Federico Valeri <fedevaleri@gmail.com> wrote:

> Hello devs, we would like to start a vote for KIP-1279: Cluster Mirroring.
>
>
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1279%3A+Cluster+Mirroring
>
> This KIP proposes natively integrating asynchronous cross-cluster
> replication directly into Kafka brokers. It enables instant client
> failovers without messy offset translation, supports incremental
> failbacks, and makes bridge-less KRaft migrations much easier to
> manage.
>
> Thanks
> Fede
>

