Matthias J. Sax created KAFKA-20808:
---------------------------------------

             Summary: StreamThread dies with fatal InvalidStateStoreExcepti=
on after TaskCorruptedException
                 Key: KAFKA-20808
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20808
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: streams
    Affects Versions: 4.3.0
            Reporter: Matthias J. Sax


First KafkaStreams hits an error opening a store (this code was added via K=
IP-1035, and triggers only via EOS)
{code:java}
Caused by: org.apache.kafka.streams.errors.ProcessorStateException: State s=
tore example-window-store-v1.1700000000000 didn't find a valid state, since=
 under EOS it has the risk of getting uncommitted data in stores=09... 37 c=
ommon frames omitted
    Caused by: org.apache.kafka.streams.errors.ProcessorStateException: Inv=
alid state during store open. Expected state to be either empty or closed
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.AbstractColumnFamilyAccessor=
.open(AbstractColumnFamilyAccessor.java:93)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.RocksDBStore.openDB(RocksDBS=
tore.java:263){code}
The error is converted into a TaskCorruptedException and KafkaStreams try t=
o close the task dirty, and re-initialize it, but fails with
{code:java}
org.apache.kafka.streams.errors.InvalidStateStoreException: Store example-w=
indow-store-v1.1700000000000 is currently closed
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.RocksDBStore.validateStoreOp=
en(RocksDBStore.java:472)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.RocksDBStore.committedOffset=
(RocksDBStore.java:745)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.AbstractSegments.committedOf=
fset(AbstractSegments.java:196)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.AbstractRocksDBSegmentedByte=
sStore.committedOffset(AbstractRocksDBSegmentedBytesStore.java:329)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.WrappedStateStore.committedO=
ffset(WrappedStateStore.java:153)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.WrappedStateStore.committedO=
ffset(WrappedStateStore.java:153)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.WrappedStateStore.committedO=
ffset(WrappedStateStore.java:153)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.ProcessorStateManager.in=
itializeStoreOffsets(ProcessorStateManager.java:308)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StateManagerUtil.registe=
rStateStores(StateManagerUtil.java:150)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StandbyTask.initializeIf=
Needed(StandbyTask.java:112)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.TaskManager.addTaskToSta=
teUpdater(TaskManager.java:949)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.TaskManager.addTasksToSt=
ateUpdater(TaskManager.java:934)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.TaskManager.checkStateUp=
dater(TaskManager.java:848)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StreamThread.checkStateU=
pdater(StreamThread.java:1409)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StreamThread.runOnceWith=
outProcessingThreads(StreamThread.java:1235)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StreamThread.runLoop(Str=
eamThread.java:956)
=09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StreamThread.run(StreamT=
hread.java:916)"} {code}
=C2=A0

Root cause:

When a segmented store fails to open a segment during openExisting under EO=
S, the task is closed dirty and revived as intended, but the retry dies fat=
ally instead of recovering. Root cause is a stale, unopened segment left in=
 the in-memory AbstractSegments.segments map that the dirty-close never cle=
ars.

Mechanism
1. AbstractSegments.getOrCreateSegment inserts the segment into the map (:9=
5) before openSegmentDB (:99) =E2=80=94 long-standing (KAFKA-3522).
2. Under EOS the open now throws TaskCorruptedException via the OPEN/closed=
 status-key check (AbstractColumnFamilyAccessor.open:107 =E2=86=92 RocksDBS=
tore.openDB:279). This fires inside AbstractRocksDBSegmentedBytesStore.init=
 at segments.openExisting (:313) =E2=80=94 before stateStoreContext.registe=
r(...) (:319).
3. Because the store was never registered, ProcessorStateManager.close() (c=
loses only registered stores, :666) skips it, so AbstractSegments.close()/s=
egments.clear() (:205/:209) never runs. The unopened segment (open=3D=3Dfal=
se) survives closeDirty.
4. On revive+retry, openExisting short-circuits on segments.containsKey (:9=
0-91) and returns the stale segment without reopening; init completes and r=
egisters the store.
5. ProcessorStateManager.initializeStoreOffsets then calls committedOffset =
(:345), which iterates segments (AbstractSegments:196) and calls validateSt=
oreOpen on the stale one =E2=86=92 fatal InvalidStateStoreException (RocksD=
BStore:894=E2=86=92:478) =E2=86=92 caught as generic StreamsException (Stre=
amThread:1039, not the TaskCorruptedException branch at :1004) =E2=86=92 SH=
UTDOWN_CLIENT.

While the code in AbstractSegments.getOrCreateSegment is old, it could not =
trip before, because no TaskCorruptedException was throw on this code path.=
 This only change with KIP-1035.



