Matthias J. Sax resolved KAFKA-20808.
-------------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

> StreamThread dies with fatal InvalidStateStoreException after TaskCorrupt=
edException
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-20808
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20808
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Bug
>          Components: streams
>    Affects Versions: 4.3.0
>            Reporter: Matthias J. Sax
>            Assignee: Matthias J. Sax
>            Priority: Critical
>             Fix For: 4.4.0, 4.3.2
>
>
> First KafkaStreams hits an error opening a store (this code was added via=
 KIP-1035, and triggers only via EOS)
> {code:java}
> Caused by: org.apache.kafka.streams.errors.ProcessorStateException: State=
 store example-window-store-v1.1700000000000 didn't find a valid state, sin=
ce under EOS it has the risk of getting uncommitted data in stores
> =09... 37 common frames omitted
>     Caused by: org.apache.kafka.streams.errors.ProcessorStateException: I=
nvalid state during store open. Expected state to be either empty or closed
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.AbstractColumnFamilyAccess=
or.open(AbstractColumnFamilyAccessor.java:93)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.RocksDBStore.openDB(RocksD=
BStore.java:263){code}
> The error is converted into a TaskCorruptedException and KafkaStreams try=
 to close the task dirty, and re-initialize it, but fails with
> {code:java}
> org.apache.kafka.streams.errors.InvalidStateStoreException: Store example=
-window-store-v1.1700000000000 is currently closed
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.RocksDBStore.validateStore=
Open(RocksDBStore.java:472)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.RocksDBStore.committedOffs=
et(RocksDBStore.java:745)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.AbstractSegments.committed=
Offset(AbstractSegments.java:196)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.AbstractRocksDBSegmentedBy=
tesStore.committedOffset(AbstractRocksDBSegmentedBytesStore.java:329)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.WrappedStateStore.committe=
dOffset(WrappedStateStore.java:153)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.WrappedStateStore.committe=
dOffset(WrappedStateStore.java:153)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.state.internals.WrappedStateStore.committe=
dOffset(WrappedStateStore.java:153)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.ProcessorStateManager.=
initializeStoreOffsets(ProcessorStateManager.java:308)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StateManagerUtil.regis=
terStateStores(StateManagerUtil.java:150)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StandbyTask.initialize=
IfNeeded(StandbyTask.java:112)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.TaskManager.addTaskToS=
tateUpdater(TaskManager.java:949)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.TaskManager.addTasksTo=
StateUpdater(TaskManager.java:934)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.TaskManager.checkState=
Updater(TaskManager.java:848)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StreamThread.checkStat=
eUpdater(StreamThread.java:1409)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StreamThread.runOnceWi=
thoutProcessingThreads(StreamThread.java:1235)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StreamThread.runLoop(S=
treamThread.java:956)
> =09at org.apache.kafka.streams.processor.internals.StreamThread.run(Strea=
mThread.java:916)"} {code}
> =C2=A0
> *Root cause:*
> When a segmented store fails to open a segment during openExisting under =
EOS, the task is closed dirty and revived as intended, but the retry dies f=
atally instead of recovering. Root cause is a stale, unopened segment left =
in the in-memory AbstractSegments.segments map that the dirty-close never c=
lears.
> *Mechanism:*
> 1. AbstractSegments.getOrCreateSegment inserts the segment into the map (=
:95) before openSegmentDB (:99) =E2=80=94 long-standing (KAFKA-3522).
> 2. Under EOS the open now throws TaskCorruptedException via the OPEN/clos=
ed status-key check (AbstractColumnFamilyAccessor.open:107 =E2=86=92 RocksD=
BStore.openDB:279). This fires inside AbstractRocksDBSegmentedBytesStore.in=
it at segments.openExisting (:313) =E2=80=94 before stateStoreContext.regis=
ter(...) (:319).
> 3. Because the store was never registered, ProcessorStateManager.close() =
(closes only registered stores, :666) skips it, so AbstractSegments.close()=
/segments.clear() (:205/:209) never runs. The unopened segment (open=3D=3Df=
alse) survives closeDirty.
> 4. On revive+retry, openExisting short-circuits on segments.containsKey (=
:90-91) and returns the stale segment without reopening; init completes and=
 registers the store.
> 5. ProcessorStateManager.initializeStoreOffsets then calls committedOffse=
t (:345), which iterates segments (AbstractSegments:196) and calls validate=
StoreOpen on the stale one =E2=86=92 fatal InvalidStateStoreException (Rock=
sDBStore:894=E2=86=92:478) =E2=86=92 caught as generic StreamsException (St=
reamThread:1039, not the TaskCorruptedException branch at :1004) =E2=86=92 =
SHUTDOWN_CLIENT.
> While the code in AbstractSegments.getOrCreateSegment is old, it could no=
t trip before, because no TaskCorruptedException was throw on this code pat=
h. This only change with KIP-1035.



