hi all,

I re-read the constructors, and I think deprecating the time-accepting constr=
uctors will introduce huge changes to the codebase.

Maybe we could just make Time public with a few methods, such as milliseconds=
, nanoseconds, and sleep. Since Timer is not public, we could add a helper me=
thod to Timer, like Timer.create(Time, ...), to replace Time#timer().

WDYT?

On 2026/04/23 20:57:19 Siddhartha Devineni wrote:
