Hi all, thanks for the KIP.

The motivation for addressing this improvement in this shape (client-side
metrics) is not too clear to me, mainly given how the rebalance landscape
has changed drastically (KIP-848 GA).

I do get that the way to troubleshoot rebalances with the classic consumer
is troublesome (based on client logs), visibility limited etc, but the
problem is actually much bigger than that, and that's why the new Consumer
protocol (KIP-848) was delivered and changed the whole experience around
rebalances (including visibility). Then, with KIP-848, rebalances are
driven by the coordinator, so I would expect that if there
are visibility gaps we should better address them on the broker side? (e.g,
more metrics if needed?).

Also there is a clear timeline to make the new Consumer protocol default
for the KafkaConsumer and eventually deprecate the classic consumer
(KIP-1274), so we should keep that in mind, just to better assess/target
the investment.

Was this considered? Thoughts?

Thanks!
Lianet


